<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78464" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρᾰνᾱλ-ίσκω</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρᾰνᾱλ-όω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ανᾱλώσω</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spend amiss, waste, squander, throw away</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραναλώσετε πάνθ᾽ ὅσ᾽ ἂν δαπανήσητε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					<u>Prooem.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῶν ἰδίων π. εἰς οὐδὲν δέον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					13.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				3.7.13
			</span></i> ; <i>ruin</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν πόλιν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.21.7
			</span></i> :—
				Pass.
			, of persons, <i>to be sacrificed incidentally</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραναλώθησαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				14.5
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολώλαμεν, παρανηλώμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Nu.</u>
					17.12(27)
				</span></i>
			 : in Com., <i>to be spent incidentally</i>, pres.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραναλούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					164.5
				</span></i>
			 : pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραναλωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arched.
					2.11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
